      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143475",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{7}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cExp(\u03b8)$ and unknown rate parameter $\u03b8$. For a particular sample $x_{1}, x_{2}, \u2026, x_{7}$, you're given that\n$\u2211_(i = 1)^(7)x_{i} = 18.2$.\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n*Hint: The probability density function for an exponential random variable is given by*\n$f(x; \u03b8) = \u03b8e^{- \u03b8x}, x \\ge 0$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
